# ------------------------------------------------------------
#  Password file for nginx basic auth.
#  Save this file as  .htpasswd  (in C:\fileshare\conf\).
#
#  One account per line, in the form:   username:password
#  Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#
#  On Windows, nginx accepts a PLAIN-TEXT password here, so the
#  simplest option is just to type the password. Example:
#
#      john:MySecret123
#
#  Prefer a hashed password instead? Replace the part after ':'
#  with an apr1 hash (works on Windows too). You can generate it
#  with Git-for-Windows' openssl:
#
#      openssl passwd -apr1 MySecret123
#      ->  $apr1$xxxxxxxx$yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy
#
#  then write:   john:$apr1$xxxxxxxx$yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy
# ------------------------------------------------------------

# Replace the line below with your own username:password
john:change-me
